mpts and auto-accept while composing, without relying on an ambiguous icon state."},{"Sha":"981353793d47280973f46022292f2e8dd7dfd681","Login":"iamdavidhill","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"David Hill","AuthorEmail":"iamdavidhill@gmail.com","Date":"2026-03-08T00:47:21+00:00","Message":"tui: add more editor bottom padding for prompt controls\n\nGives typed text more breathing room above the Add file/model/thinking row so the controls don\u2019t visually crowd what you\u2019re writing."},{"Sha":"426dcfa3b0cacc79abac6c6f61a03613b572ad64","Login":"iamdavidhill","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"David Hill","AuthorEmail":"iamdavidhill@gmail.com","Date":"2026-03-08T00:46:26+00:00","Message":"tui: keep model \u002B thinking selectors beside Add file\n\nPeople change models and thinking settings while composing, so keeping those controls next to the Add file button avoids hunting in the footer and reduces context switching mid-message."},{"Sha":"69cb49f7cc6557f8d9529695d7ecc75c0ac8a5aa","Login":"iamdavidhill","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"David Hill","AuthorEmail":"iamdavidhill@gmail.com","Date":"2026-03-08T00:06:02+00:00","Message":"tui: dock auto-accept after thinking and move Add file to bottom-left\n\nAuto-accept now lives in the footer dock beside the thinking control so it stays easy to find without crowding the text box.\n\nThe Add file button moves to the bottom-left of the editor and the input gets a bit more bottom padding so the control row doesn\u2019t overlap what you\u2019re typing."},{"Sha":"e30678a088d7921a4084595ae3c83a2095dbd0f2","Login":"thdxr","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"Dax Raad","AuthorEmail":"d@ironbay.co","Date":"2026-03-08T00:47:57+00:00","Message":"test: normalize ripgrep path assertion on windows"},{"Sha":"771b29a857339cf2156d80b275888ee98ed9a708","Login":"opencode-agent[bot]","IsBot":true,"AuthorName":"opencode-agent[bot]","AuthorEmail":"opencode-agent[bot]@users.noreply.github.com","Date":"2026-03-08T00:31:35+00:00","Message":"chore: generate"},{"Sha":"e6d1aae33afc1270a94b8e26f8a520caa275ddd3","Login":"thdxr","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"Dax Raad","AuthorEmail":"d@ironbay.co","Date":"2026-03-08T00:21:22+00:00","Message":"test: lock in process, ripgrep, and installation helpers"},{"Sha":"9dc8ac47341032096e10761c570e498cc26d2ec1","Login":"iamdavidhill","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"David Hill","AuthorEmail":"iamdavidhill@gmail.com","Date":"2026-03-08T00:17:28+00:00","Message":"tui: revert prompt control docking\n\nRestore the previous prompt control layout after the dock/position changes made the composer feel less familiar.\n\nThis brings auto-accept back to its prior spot and returns Add file to the previous placement."},{"Sha":"fdd037ba204126c37bd175ace3428d35c7502619","Login":"iamdavidhill","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"David Hill","AuthorEmail":"iamdavidhill@gmail.com","Date":"2026-03-08T00:06:02+00:00","Message":"tui: dock auto-accept after thinking and move Add file to bottom-left\n\nAuto-accept now lives in the footer dock beside the thinking control so it stays easy to find without crowding the text box.\n\nThe Add file button moves to the bottom-left of the editor and the input gets a bit more bottom padding so the control row doesn\u2019t overlap what you\u2019re typing."},{"Sha":"523f792b486fb7c3cbcc15fa882dd953af31428e","Login":"thdxr","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"Dax Raad","AuthorEmail":"d@ironbay.co","Date":"2026-03-07T23:52:35+00:00","Message":"core: update database path test to verify correct channel-based filename\n\nThe test now validates that the database file is named according to the current installation channel (latest/beta get \u0027opencode.db\u0027, others get sanitized names). This ensures users\u0027 data is stored in the correct location based on their update channel."},{"Sha":"2230c3c40136746c88e781cff613037e6d958d8e","Login":"thdxr","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"Dax Raad","AuthorEmail":"d@ironbay.co","Date":"2026-03-07T23:48:13+00:00","Message":"core: allow beta channel to share database with stable channel"},{"Sha":"1b494e508714275737417315f09bcf79d25cbc65","Login":"iamdavidhill","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"David Hill","AuthorEmail":"iamdavidhill@gmail.com","Date":"2026-03-07T23:50:23+00:00","Message":"tui: balance titlebar columns so center content doesn\u0027t get squeezed by long side content"},{"Sha":"9c43893a0fce1789c4381b28b30366cb60dcca66","Login":"iamdavidhill","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"David Hill","AuthorEmail":"iamdavidhill@gmail.com","Date":"2026-03-07T23:49:10+00:00","Message":"tui: align numeric displays consistently across tool outputs and diff counters using tabular numerals"},{"Sha":"6dfe19b44549ed844e233f3321cb23833098cbca","Login":"iamdavidhill","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"David Hill","AuthorEmail":"iamdavidhill@gmail.com","Date":"2026-03-07T23:45:16+00:00","Message":"tui: center empty states vertically in session view and improve review panel messaging for projects without version control"},{"Sha":"a965a062595403a8e0083e85770315d5dc9628ab","Login":"thdxr","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"Dax Raad","AuthorEmail":"d@ironbay.co","Date":"2026-03-07T21:17:00+00:00","Message":"core: add OPENCODE_SKIP_MIGRATIONS flag to bypass database migrations\n\nAllows users to skip automatic database migrations by setting the\nOPENCODE_SKIP_MIGRATIONS environment variable. Useful for testing\nscenarios or when manually managing database state."},{"Sha":"0654f28c7296cf31de10a6399bf82d43ef626202","Login":"fwang","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"Frank","AuthorEmail":"frank@anoma.ly","Date":"2026-03-07T19:27:51+00:00","Message":"zen: fix graph legend"},{"Sha":"a32b76dee0595cdce935e702bb8ede0956e5cc16","Login":"adamdotdevin","IsBot":false,"AuthorName":"Adam","AuthorEmail":"2363879\u002Badamdotdevin@users.noreply.github.com","Date":"2026-03-07T19:27:40+00:00","Message":"fix(app): review panel transition"},{"Sha":"a52d640c8c56a5d9fb4623a1c601046c3d9a37b7","Login":null,"IsBot":true,"AuthorName":"opencode","AuthorEmail":"opencode@sst.dev","Date":"2026-03-07T18:00:39+00:00","